t protocol is also complete: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disconnection, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered mount, LV, and data state. The final boot ID agrees with the fixed after-executor observation.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the boot transition and general node hygiene but do not probe the LVM or /srv/data mount; final storage-state confirmation therefore relies on captured executor commands.","Two earlier reboot validations exposed nonpersistent mounting configurations before the final corrected restart protocol succeeded."]}
